- Tech stack: React (Vite), TypeScript, Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Firebase Auth, Cloud Firestore, Firebase Storage, Firebase Cloud Functions, pnpm, Node.js, Firebase Admin SDK
- Frontend source lives in `src/`. Backend/server-side code lives in `cloud-functions/src/`.
- Use `pnpm add` when installing new packages.
- Use `npx shadcn@latest add` to add new shadcn components.
- You are not able to see or modify .env files directly - so tell the user what they should add to the file if needed.
- Avoid classes/OOP and use a functional reusable component programming style.
- Do not add Supabase, Drizzle, Hono, or tRPC.
- When Firestore rules or indexes change, edit the committed rules/index files; do not apply production schema changes yourself.
- Default local auth is `src/data/local-auth.json` (DEV only). Set `VITE_AUTH_MODE=firebase` when using Firebase Auth/Firestore.
- Default seed is the Firebase Emulator via `pnpm seed`. Seed production only when explicitly asked, then give `pnpm seed:prod` (requires ALLOW_PRODUCTION_SEED=true).
- Never run git commit or git push. Give the user the commands, split into multiple logical commits, then an optional git push.
- Never commit files from the ./docs/features folder
